+initial sync. If the server reports that the existing installation authorization was revoked (401 or
+403, including account deletion), `connect` removes that authorization and auxiliary automatic state
+through the normal lifecycle cleanup, then starts fresh pairing without requiring `disconnect` or an
+abandoned pairing. Stable installation and local source identities and discovery are retained. The
+final token/config swap is serialized behind any active sync, so an older request cannot restore
+superseded authorization; other reconciliation or network errors retain the previous connection.
 
